# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EVALUATION BOUNDARY — the blind corpus
#
# Nothing that states expected behaviour, or names/describes a planted defect,
# for the BLIND corpus (test-suite/blind/) may enter the public repo.
#
# The rules below are UNCONDITIONAL. Which *tiers* ship at all was decided by
# the owner and is applied at the end of this file as PHASE 1 OF A STAGGERED
# PUSH — see the block headed "PHASE 1" and docs/EVALUATION-BOUNDARY.md.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED — these belong to the OPEN corpus, are published on
# purpose, and the scorer suites read them:
#   test-suite/branching/**/manifest.flawed.json  (seeded patches, open corpus)
#   scorer/oracle/generated/*.{clean,flawed}.json (derived oracles, open corpus)
#   scorer/test/calibration-pins.mjs              (pinned calibration constants)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# blind-test answer keys: kept out of the public repo so the corpus stays blind
test-suite/blind/**/truth/
test-suite/blind/**/*.answerkey.json

# belt-and-braces: these filenames only ever mean "disclosure of expected
# behaviour", wherever someone puts them (including outside truth/)
**/answer-key.json
**/answer-key.*.json
**/*.answerkey.json
**/ANSWER-KEY.md
**/seeded-defects.json
**/seeded-defects.*.json
# corpus100 truth artifacts: obligations.json records site_satisfies per requirement
# and ambiguities.json records which cases are deliberately unresolvable — both are
# answer keys wherever they are put, not only inside truth/.
**/obligations.json
**/ambiguities.json
**/seeded-patch*.json
**/adjudication*.json
**/adjudications/
**/calibration-results*.json
**/*.oracle.json
test-suite/blind/**/oracle*
test-suite/blind/**/METHOD.md
test-suite/blind/**/*expected*
test-suite/blind/**/*defect*

# Runs, judgements and rendered reports DERIVED from a blind tier reconstruct
# that tier's corpus and its planted defects from captured artifacts alone.
# Tiers 2-4 are excluded here; t1-easy-derived output is excluded in the PHASE 1
# block at the end of this file, for the same reason.
pipeline/runs/t2-*/
pipeline/runs/t3-*/
pipeline/runs/t4-*/
pipeline/judge/out/t2-*/
pipeline/judge/out/t3-*/
pipeline/judge/out/t4-*/
pipeline/report/samples/t2-*
pipeline/report/samples/t3-*
pipeline/report/samples/t4-*
worker-v2/ui/fixtures/*-t2-*.json
worker-v2/ui/fixtures/*-t3-*.json
worker-v2/ui/fixtures/*-t4-*.json

# deploy runbook with real account/app ids — sanitize before publishing
worker-v2/DEPLOY-READY.md

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PHASE 1 OF A STAGGERED PUSH — NOT A PERMANENT EXCLUSION
#
# OWNER'S RULING: "just keep the testing material blind for now, and once the
# test runs are complete, publish them alongside the test materials on the repo
# — staggered push."
#
# So: the blind corpus AND everything derived from it stay out of the public
# repository UNTIL the test runs are complete, and then go in TOGETHER with the
# results. Everything listed below is intended to be PUBLISHED LATER. If you are
# reading this after the runs finished, the exclusion has expired — see
# docs/EVALUATION-BOUNDARY.md for exactly what phase 2 involves.
#
# WHY THE DERIVED OUTPUT HAD TO GO TOO. Excluding test-suite/blind/ alone
# accomplishes nothing: pipeline/runs/t1-easy reconstructs the t1 corpus and
# every seeded defect from captured artifacts on their own (_textdiff.json
# carries a verbatim doc-vs-site copy of every screen; _analysis.json prints the
# full option inventory with codes; the session traces carry each mis-route).
#
# WHAT REPLACES IT FOR THE PUBLIC TEST SUITES. `pipeline/runs/synthetic-demo/`
# — a signed, multi-session run over an invented houseplant questionnaire, built
# by pipeline/runs/make-synthetic-run.mjs and resolved by
# pipeline/runs/run-source.mjs. It is committed on purpose. Suites that need
# "a real signed run" use it; the handful of tests that assert t1-easy's own
# content skip with a stated reason and a printed banner, never silently.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
test-suite/blind/

# t1-easy-derived output (reconstructs the corpus and its planted defects)
pipeline/runs/t1-easy/
pipeline/judge/out/t1-easy/
pipeline/judge/replay/
pipeline/judge/VERIFICATION.md
pipeline/judge/VERIFICATION-ROUND2.md
pipeline/judge/VERIFICATION-ROUND3.md
pipeline/report/samples/acceptance/
pipeline/report/samples/t1-easy-as-run.html
pipeline/report/samples/t1-easy-current-results.html
pipeline/report/samples/t1-easy-register.html
pipeline/report/samples/t1-easy.flag-lanes.json
worker-v2/ui/fixtures/16-live-seeded-t1-easy.json
# ...and the preview RENDERED from that fixture. The rule above covered only the
# JSON; the HTML is the same content laid out for reading, so it reconstructs the
# seeded run just as well. Same rationale, same expiry.
worker-v2/ui/previews/16-live-seeded-t1-easy.html

# v2 acceptance output captured at the repo root: run-record.v2.json and
# contract-revision.json for a t1-easy run. These are exactly the "captured
# artifacts" the banner above says reconstruct the corpus and its planted
# defects — a run record is the most disclosive single file we produce.
/v2-acceptance-*/

# THE HOSTED SURVEY SITE ITSELF. targets/t1-easy-host/ is the deployed copy of a
# blind tier's instrument: the seeded site is half the answer key in executable
# form (public/survey.js carries the routing the document is checked against, and
# verify-log.json records what was served). t1-easy is retired, so this exclusion
# is conservative rather than urgent — but the RULE it establishes is not:
#
#   RULE FOR THE NEXT SURVEY HOSTED THIS WAY: a target site built for a blind
#   tier is blind material and is excluded from the moment it is created, in the
#   same commit that creates it. It ships in phase 2 with the corpus and the
#   results, never before and never separately. Host it under targets/ so this
#   rule keeps matching.
targets/

# The PUBLIC stand-in run is deliberately NOT excluded — the five suites above
# depend on it and it contains nothing derived from the blind corpus.
!pipeline/runs/synthetic-demo/

# Newer mixed source/generated roots are quarantined for this sprint. They are not required
# by the accepted experiment and cannot be safely bulk-staged while captures and source are
# intermingled. Split and boundary-review any source before publishing it.
/bakeoff/
/bakeoff-extract/

# Generated spike and document-robustness evidence.
/graph-spike/out/
/graph-spike/arm/out/
/test-suite/docx-robustness/out/
/test-suite/docx-robustness/corpus/_probes-*.json

# Private sprint inputs/results publish only at the explicit staggered release trigger.
/sprint/private/
/sprint/runs/
/sprint/04-CORPUS.md

# Known contaminated working note and local IDE/session material.
/docs/ITERATION-LOOP.md
/.claude/
/.local-private/

